llvm-4.0.0 backport patch: LoopStrengthReduce counts an immediate once per run of equal fixup offsets (PS4)

This patch CHANGES CODE GENERATION for a loop whose address uses share a
non-zero offset. r278927 (Jonas Paulsson, 2016-08-17, "[LoopStrenghtReduce]
Refactoring and addition of a new target cost function", llvm-project
7a79422536d8, D19152, first release LLVM 4.0) made an LSRUse own its fixups
and removed the use's Offsets list; Cost::RateFormula then adds the
immediate's cost once per fixup where 3.9 added it once per entry of that
list, which held a run of equal offsets once. With three accesses at -4 the
4.0.0 cost picks a zero-displacement base and an exit compare (`cmp rbx,
-4`); 3.9.1 and the base keep the -4 displacement and exit on the add's
flags (`add rbx, -4; jne`). In the game region 53 array-destroy loops over
ten or more names have the base's form (round 181A's census, round 185A's
probe: no source form of the element's destructor changes the exit; the
prebuilt 3.9.1 gives the base's bytes, 4.0.0 and 5.0.2 do not). With this
patch 12 of those loops compile to the base's bytes (none before) and no
matched game row and no draft changes (round 186B's module sweep, repeated
by the supervisor). The rest of r278927 (the fixups' ownership, the target
cost hook) stays.

--- a/lib/Transforms/Scalar/LoopStrengthReduce.cpp
+++ b/lib/Transforms/Scalar/LoopStrengthReduce.cpp
@@ -1184,10 +1184,21 @@
   ScaleCost += getScalingFactorCost(TTI, LU, F);
 
   // Tally up the non-zero immediates.
+  // PS4: an immediate is counted once per run of fixups with the same
+  // offset, as 3.9's LSRUse::Offsets list had it; r278927 (a use owns its
+  // fixups, the Offsets vector removed), which counts it once per fixup, is
+  // not taken.
+  bool HavePrevOffset = false;
+  int64_t PrevOffset = 0;
   for (const LSRFixup &Fixup : LU.Fixups) {
     int64_t O = Fixup.Offset;
     int64_t Offset = (uint64_t)O + F.BaseOffset;
-    if (F.BaseGV)
+    bool NewOffset = !HavePrevOffset || O != PrevOffset;
+    HavePrevOffset = true;
+    PrevOffset = O;
+    if (!NewOffset)
+      ; // counted with the fixup before it
+    else if (F.BaseGV)
       ImmCost += 64; // Handle symbolic values conservatively.
                      // TODO: This should probably be the pointer size.
     else if (Offset != 0)
